## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite project.

### Changes Made

1. **Installed @vercel/analytics package** (v2.0.1)
   - Added as a production dependency in package.json
   - Updated package-lock.json with new dependencies

2. **Modified src/App.jsx**
   - Imported Analytics component from '@vercel/analytics/react'
   - Added <Analytics /> component to the App component's return statement
   - Placed Analytics component after Footer to ensure proper tracking across all routes

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation for React applications:
- Used the React-specific import path: `@vercel/analytics/react`
- Added the Analytics component at the root App level to track all pages
- Positioned after all content to avoid affecting initial render performance

### Verification

✅ Build completed successfully (npm run build)
✅ Linter passed with no errors (npm run lint)
✅ All dependencies properly installed
✅ Package lock file updated

### Next Steps

To enable analytics tracking:
1. Deploy this project to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
3. Analytics will automatically begin tracking page views and web vitals

The Analytics component will automatically detect the production environment and send data when deployed on Vercel.
